    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "### Issue / context (if applicable)\n\nThe session database is the only copy of a conversation, but three code paths rewrote persisted tool output to shrink context. A cleared output renders as `[Old tool result content cleared]`, and `history get` returns the rewritten data, so neither history nor a script reading the database could serve as a source of truth. Spec: `docs/compose/spec/lossless-session-db.md`.\n\n### Type of change\n\nRefactor\n\n### What does this PR do?\n\nAfter this change no code path mutates a persisted part to reduce context size; context size is controlled only by window boundaries.\n\n- Remove turn-end `prune` and `stripNonEssential` (`session/prune.ts`) and their call in `session/prompt.ts`. It only ran with an explicit `compaction.prune: true` (unset meant off, although the docs said \"default true\"), on a cold cache, for main-agent messages.\n- Remove the uncalled `SessionCompaction.prune`, its wrapper and interface member.\n- Remove the rebuild-time microcompact in `insertRebuildBoundary`.\n- Remove `pressureLevel` / `contextPressureLevel`, `Flag.MIMOCODE_DISABLE_PRUNE`, and the `compaction.prune` config key (schema, docs row, generated SDK type). A config that still contains the key loads normally: `normalizeLoadedConfig` drops it with one warning, like `auto_worktree`.\n- `fireCheckpoints`, the threshold functions and `resetThresholds` are unchanged.\n- Legacy rows that already carry `time.compacted` keep rendering the cleared marker; `history get` returns their stored text.\n\nBehavior: with the default configuration nothing changes at turn end. Users who opted in to `compaction.prune` keep old outputs verbatim until the next boundary, so checkpoints trigger earlier. After a rebuild, tool outputs in messages that stay in the request are sent in full, so the first request after a rebuild can be larger.\n\n### How did you verify your code works?\n\nFrom `packages/cli`:\n\n- `bun typecheck` PASS; `packages/sdk` `bun run typecheck` PASS.\n- New/affected tests: `turn-end-lossless`, `rebuild-boundary-lossless`, `legacy-compacted-row`, `config` (\"ignores removed compaction.prune with one warning\"), `prune`, `checkpoint-thresholds`, `overflow` — 177 pass / 0 fail.\n- `turn-end-lossless` and `rebuild-boundary-lossless` were confirmed to fail on the base commit (4e58a80184) in a scratch worktree and pass on this branch.\n- Full `bun test`: 6118 pass / 79 fail / 41 skip. Every failing file (MCP, project, worktree, cron-bridge, revert-compact, tool-fail-cascade, tool-gate-cancel, apply_patch, spawn-notification) passes when run alone; the timing-dependent MCP failure in `prompt-effect.test.ts` reproduces with base sources. These are pre-existing cross-file interferences.\n\n### Screenshots / recordings\n\nN/A\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [x] I have tested my changes locally\n- [x] I have not included unrelated changes in this PR\n",
